> I had thought of this, but assumed that selling it would be some kind
> of violation of the spirit of keeping it in the public domain.

That thought also occured to me.  However, the way I think of it is that if 
it's being offered at cost, the information itself is still free, and the 
costs are merely for the transmission medium (i.e., paper and printing).  
Which isn't that different from the current state, where we can download it 
for nothing but still have to pay for our internet connections.

